//? Title: InfoGAN: Generated Codes and a Separate Recognizer
//? Subtitle: Explicit D–Q–G writes, unit-Gaussian recognition and weak MNIST samples
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A small InfoGAN fits 1000 balanced MNIST images using a generated ten-way category,
two uniform continuous codes and sixteen Gaussian noise coordinates. None of the real
digit labels enters fitting. G produces sigmoid pixels; image-only D predicts a source
logit; independent image-only Q predicts the generated category and continuous means.
Three Adam states perform D, then Q, then a fresh G write, 96 times per store and 288
writes in total. A fixed third epoch supplies the final checkpoint. The complete editable
native program preserves every original artifact, including weak grey images, category
recovery .115 and a negative empirical variational score. Small algebra examples,
exact prior words, separate G partials, full code traversals and independent numerical
checks explain the computations without claiming semantic disentanglement or convergence.
)
\toc

> Codes are generated inputs and recognition targets

G receives Gaussian noise z, a one-hot generated category c and continuous codes u.
D receives an image alone, on real and fake branches. Q receives a generated image alone;
c and u become targets in its recognition loss R. Q has its own parameters, separate from
D. G minimizes non-saturating source loss plus R, while Q minimizes R itself.

The information objective follows [Chen et al., InfoGAN (2016)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03657).
This report retains the repository's dense teaching variant: independent Q, fixed unit
recognition variance, weight one for R and explicit D–Q–G writes. The paper commonly
shares convolutional features between D and Q; those are not this small architecture.
No prior category is assigned a digit meaning or matched to a true MNIST label.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/infogan_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(52, 1250);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle s;
  s.width     = 7.5;
  s.height    = 3.;
  s.font_size = 28;
  d.node("real", {-15, 9}, "Real pixels784", s)
      .node("dr", {15, 9}, "Shared image-only D\nRaw source logit", s)
      .node("codes", {-15, 0}, "Noise16 + category10\n+ continuous2", s)
      .node("g", {-5, 0}, "Independent G\ntanh32 → sigmoid784", s)
      .node("fake", {5, 0}, "Generated pixels784", s)
      .node("df", {15, 0}, "Same D parameters", s)
      .node("q", {5, -9}, "Independent Q\ntanh32; six leaves", s)
      .node("heads", {15, -9}, "Category logits10\nContinuous means2", s)
      .edge("real", "dr")
