> Native MNIST preparation and three separate small networks

The native `mnist-assets` recipe prepares the saliency pools:1000 fitting,200 validation,
and200 held-out test images. Each true digit contributes100/20/20 observations. The loader
checks source IDs, original train/test boundaries, disjoint pools, shape and Float32[0,1]
scaling. True labels are used only for balance checks and this preview. They do not enter
G,D,Q or any fitting loss. The preview retains the first two fitting images for every digit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/infogan_pools.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto home   = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home());
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", home);
  auto                      pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(home / "saliency");
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  auto                      labels = pools[0].labels.to_vector<std::int32_t>();
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) {
    int count = 0;
    for (std::int64_t row = 0; row < 1000 && count < 2; ++row)
      if (labels[row] == c) {
        rows.push_back(row);
        ++count;
      }
  }
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), "build/infogan_pools.png", 2, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
  std::print(
      "| pool | rows | each true digit | role |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| fitting |1000|100| Adam "
      "writes |\n| validation |200|20| logs only |\n| test |200|20| fixed final diagnostics |\n");
}
