\caption(Ten rows correspond to true digits 0 through9, two fitting images per row. Those labels do not supervise this model.)
\alttext(A balanced ten-row preview shows two native MNIST examples per true digit.)

| Store | Mapping; hidden before heads | Leaves | Values | Seed |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| G | concat(z16,onehot10,u2)→tanh32→sigmoid784 |4|26800|5303|
| D | image784→tanh32→raw source1 |4|25153|5309|
| Q | image784→tanh32→category 10, then continuous2 means |6|25516|5317|
| Total | Three distinct parameter stores |14|77469|—|

Each layer creates W before b. Q's category head precedes its continuous head in the
initializer stream. Q predicts unbounded linear means, not clipped codes or fitted
variances. The canonical tanh/sigmoid map, raw source score and categorical CE are reused;
there is no second implementation of their numerical algebra in this report.

> Complete fitting loop: D, then Q, then a fresh G objective

Write r=D(x),f=D(G(z,c,u)). D minimizes mean sp(-r)+mean sp(f), with stable softplus sp.
Q minimizes R above. G minimizes mean sp(-f)+R, with weight one on recognition and
without subtracting fixed prior entropy from its reported loss. All three stores have
independent Adam states with learning rate .0002,β1=.5,β2=.999,ε=1e-8.

BatchOrder(1000,32,5369) visits every fitting row once per epoch:31 full batches and an
eight-row tail. Fitting noise seeds 5364/5365/5366 pair with prior seeds 5382/5383/5384.
Validation noise/prior use5323/5347; test uses5333/5351. The third epoch is fixed in advance.
Validation logs do not select weights or an epoch. The initial test forward is archived
as an explicit diagnostic control; test outcomes never choose writes, hyperparameters,
noise banks, schedule or checkpoint weights.

The editable program prepares data, owns all three optimizers, performs all 288 writes,
restores every checkpoint tensor and tests immutable inference. The first minibatch also
archives G's source and recognition partials separately and verifies that a D-only write
leaves Q's partial bit exact with G fixed. Every selected phase recomputes its own forward.
The native full forward returns fifteen live fields; O(N²) MMD is added explicitly during
evaluation. No compiled experiment runner or legacy model helper hides orchestration.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/infogan_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <chrono>
#include <cmath>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>

namespace nn = dm::nn;
namespace m  = nn::models;
using Arrays = std::map<std::string, nn::Tensor>;
using nn::Tensor;

namespace {
void Require(bool condition, const std::string& message) {
  if (!condition)
    throw std::runtime_error(message);
}
void SaveArrays(const std::string& path, const Arrays& a) {
  nn::save_npz(path, nn::NamedTensors(a.begin(), a.end()));
}
bool Equal(const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
  return nn::equal_bits(a, b);
}
bool Equal(const Arrays& a, const Arrays& b) {
  if (a.size() != b.size())
    return false;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
    if (!b.count(key) || !Equal(value, b.at(key)))
      return false;
  return true;
}
Tensor Gaussian(std::int64_t rows, std::int64_t width, std::uint64_t seed) {
  return nn::cast(
      m::GaussianNoise({rows, width}, 1, seed).reshape({rows, width}), nn::DType::Float32);
}
double MaxAbsDiff(const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
  return nn::max(nn::abs(nn::cast(a, nn::DType::Float64) - nn::cast(b, nn::DType::Float64))).item();
}
void Mosaic(const std::filesystem::path& path, const Tensor& image, std::int64_t columns) {
  nn::save_image_grid(
      image.reshape({image.size(0), 28, 28, 1}), path.string(), columns, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
}
Arrays Fields(const m::InfoGanOutput& o) {
  return {
      {"fake", o.fake},
      {"real_logit", o.real_logit},
      {"fake_logit", o.fake_logit},
      {"real_probability", o.real_probability},
      {"fake_probability", o.fake_probability},
      {"discriminator_loss", o.discriminator_loss},
      {"generator_loss", o.generator_loss},
      {"source_generator_loss", o.source_generator_loss},
      {"recognition_loss", o.recognition_loss},
      {"categorical_loss", o.categorical_loss},
      {"continuous_loss", o.continuous_loss},
      {"mi_lower_bound", o.mi_lower_bound},
      {"q_logits", o.q_logits},
      {"q_probability", o.q_probability},
      {"q_mean", o.q_mean}};
}

double Value(const Arrays& a, const std::string& key) {
  return a.at(key).item();
}

void SavePrior(const std::filesystem::path& path, const m::InfoCodes& codes, const Tensor& z) {
  SaveArrays(
      path.string(),
      {{"category", codes.category},
       {"continuous", codes.continuous},
       {"raw", codes.raw},
       {"z", z}});
}

} // namespace
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path root   = "build/infogan";
  const int                   epochs = 3;
  const auto                  data = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency";
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", data.parent_path());
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  const auto   pools = m::LoadSaliency(data);
  const Tensor vn = Gaussian(200, 16, 5323), tn = Gaussian(200, 16, 5333);
  const auto   vc = m::InfoPrior(200, 5347), tc = m::InfoPrior(200, 5351);
  SavePrior(root / "validation_prior.npz", vc, vn);
  SavePrior(root / "test_prior.npz", tc, tn);
  nn::ParameterStore               g(5303), d(5309), q(5317);
  std::vector<nn::ParameterStore*> stores{&g, &d, &q};
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    m::InfoGan(
        g,
        d,
        q,
        nn::zeros({2, 784}),
        nn::zeros({2, 16}),
        nn::zeros({2}, nn::DType::Int32),
        nn::zeros({2, 2}));
  }
  auto snapshot = [&]() {
    Arrays out;
    for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k)
      for (const auto& name : stores[k]->names())
        out.emplace(std::to_string(k) + "/" + name, stores[k]->at(name).detach().clone());
    return out;
  };
  auto forward = [&](const Tensor& x, const Tensor& z, const Tensor& c, const Tensor& u) {
    return Fields(m::InfoGan(g, d, q, x.reshape({x.size(0), 784}), z, c, u));
  };
  auto evaluate = [&](const Tensor& x, const Tensor& z, const Tensor& c, const Tensor& u) {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    auto            out = forward(x, z, c, u);
    out.emplace(
        "pixel_mmd", m::ImqMmd(m::GanCoarsePixels(x), m::GanCoarsePixels(out.at("fake"))).value);
    return out;
  };
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind    = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  config.beta1   = .5;
  config.beta2   = .999;
  config.epsilon = 1e-8;
  nn::Optimizer               go(g, .0002, config), disc(d, .0002, config), rec(q, .0002, config);
  std::vector<nn::Optimizer*> optimizers{&go, &disc, &rec};
  Require(
      g.count() == 26800 && d.count() == 25153 && q.count() == 25516 &&
          g.size() + d.size() + q.size() == 14,
      "77469 parameters 14 tensors");
  SaveArrays((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), snapshot());
  SaveArrays(
      (root / "initial_outputs.npz").string(),
      evaluate(pools[2].images, tn, tc.category, tc.continuous));
  nn::BatchOrder order(1000, 32, 5369);
  int            steps = 0;
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history
      << "epoch\tdiscriminator_loss\tgenerator_loss\trecognition_loss\tmi_lower_bound\tpixel_mmd\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto source  = nn::cast(pools[0].source, nn::DType::Int64).to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    const Tensor noise = Gaussian(1000, 16, 5363 + epoch);
    const auto   codes = m::InfoPrior(1000, 5381 + epoch);
    order.begin_epoch();
    int seen = 0;
    for (;;) {
      const auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      const Tensor x = nn::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), z = nn::take_rows(noise, rows),
                   c = nn::take_rows(codes.category, rows),
                   u = nn::take_rows(codes.continuous, rows);
      std::vector<Tensor> q_before;
      if (!steps) {
        SaveArrays((root / "first_forward.npz").string(), evaluate(x, z, c, u));
        Arrays partials;
        for (const std::string component :
             {"source_generator_loss", "recognition_loss", "generator_loss"}) {
          const auto values = nn::grad(forward(x, z, c, u).at(component), g.parameters());
          const auto names  = g.names();
          for (std::size_t k = 0; k < names.size(); ++k)
            partials.emplace(component + "/" + names[k], values[k]);
        }
        for (const auto& name : g.names())
          Require(
              nn::max(
                  nn::abs(
                      partials.at("generator_loss/" + name) -
                      partials.at("source_generator_loss/" + name) -
                      partials.at("recognition_loss/" + name)))
                      .item() < 2e-6,
              "G source and recognition partials sum to total");
        SaveArrays((root / "initial_g_partials.npz").string(), partials);
        q_before = nn::grad(forward(x, z, c, u).at("recognition_loss"), q.parameters());
      }
      for (int group : {1, 2, 0}) {
        const auto before = steps ? Arrays{} : snapshot();
        if (!steps && group == 2) {
          const auto after = nn::grad(forward(x, z, c, u).at("recognition_loss"), q.parameters());
          for (std::size_t k = 0; k < after.size(); ++k)
            Require(
                nn::equal_bits(q_before[k], after[k]),
                "D write leaves Q partial unchanged with G fixed");
        }
        // Every phase recomputes after the previous selected-store write.
        const auto out  = forward(x, z, c, u);
        const auto loss = out.at(
            group == 0   ? "generator_loss"
            : group == 1 ? "discriminator_loss"
                         : "recognition_loss");
        optimizers[group]->step(nn::grad(loss, stores[group]->parameters()));
        if (!steps) {
          const auto after   = snapshot();
          bool       changed = false;
          for (const auto& [key, value] : before) {
            if (key.rfind(std::to_string(group) + "/", 0) == 0)
              changed |= !nn::equal_bits(value, after.at(key));
            else
              Require(nn::equal_bits(value, after.at(key)), "unselected group unchanged");
          }
          Require(changed, "selected group changed");
        }
      }
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << steps << '\t' << row << '\t' << source[row] << '\n';
      ++steps;
      seen += int(rows.size());
    }
    Require(seen == 1000, "all 1000 fit cases once per epoch");
    const auto v = evaluate(pools[1].images, vn, vc.category, vc.continuous);
    history << epoch;
    for (auto key :
         {"discriminator_loss",
          "generator_loss",
          "recognition_loss",
          "mi_lower_bound",
          "pixel_mmd"})
      history << '\t' << Value(v, key);
    history << '\n';
    std::cout << "epoch " << epoch << ": D=" << Value(v, "discriminator_loss")
              << ", G=" << Value(v, "generator_loss")
              << ", recognition=" << Value(v, "recognition_loss")
              << ", MI bound=" << Value(v, "mi_lower_bound") << std::endl;
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();

  const auto checkpoint = (root / "final.npz").string();
  Require(
      steps == 96 && go.iterations() == 96 && disc.iterations() == 96 && rec.iterations() == 96,
      "288 D-Q-G writes");
  SaveArrays(checkpoint, snapshot());
  nn::ParameterStore restored_g(1), restored_d(2), restored_q(3);
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    m::InfoGan(
        restored_g,
        restored_d,
        restored_q,
        nn::zeros({2, 784}),
        nn::zeros({2, 16}),
        nn::zeros({2}, nn::DType::Int32),
        nn::zeros({2, 2}));
  }
  std::vector<nn::ParameterStore*> restored_stores{&restored_g, &restored_d, &restored_q};
  for (const auto& [name, value] : nn::load_npz(checkpoint))
    restored_stores.at(name[0] - '0')->set(name.substr(2), value);
  auto restored_arrays = [&]() {
    Arrays out;
    for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k)
      for (const auto& name : restored_stores[k]->names())
        out.emplace(std::to_string(k) + "/" + name, restored_stores[k]->at(name).detach().clone());
    return out;
  };
  auto sample = [&](const Tensor& z, const Tensor& c, const Tensor& u) {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    return m::InfoGanGenerate(restored_g, z, c, u);
  };
  auto restored_evaluate = [&](const Tensor& x, const Tensor& z, const Tensor& c, const Tensor& u) {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    auto            out = Fields(
        m::InfoGan(restored_g, restored_d, restored_q, x.reshape({x.size(0), 784}), z, c, u));
    out.emplace(
        "pixel_mmd", m::ImqMmd(m::GanCoarsePixels(x), m::GanCoarsePixels(out.at("fake"))).value);
    return out;
  };
  auto recognize = [&](const Tensor& image) {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    const auto      r = m::InfoGanRecognize(restored_q, image.reshape({image.size(0), 784}));
    return Arrays{{"q_probability", r.probability}, {"q_mean", r.mean}};
  };
  Require(Equal(snapshot(), restored_arrays()), "all groups restore exact");
  const auto   before = restored_arrays();
  const auto   output = restored_evaluate(pools[2].images, tn, tc.category, tc.continuous);
  const Tensor repeat = sample(tn, tc.category, tc.continuous);
  Require(Equal(repeat, output.at("fake")), "noise+codes ONLY generation exact");
  const auto recognition = recognize(repeat);
  for (auto key : {"q_probability", "q_mean"})
    Require(
        Equal(recognition.at(key), output.at(key)),
        "Q image ONLY without targets/noise/code exact");
  const double parity = MaxAbsDiff(
      sample(
          nn::take_rows(tn, {0}),
          nn::take_rows(tc.category, {0}),
          nn::take_rows(tc.continuous, {0})),
      nn::take_rows(repeat, {0}));
  Require(parity < 2e-6, "single batch parity");
  SaveArrays((root / "outputs.npz").string(), output);
  SaveArrays((root / "image_only_recognition.npz").string(), recognition);

  // Codes are sampled prior categories, not digit labels. Traversals include all outputs.
  std::vector<std::int64_t> grid_rows;
  std::vector<std::int32_t> grid_category;
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c)
    for (int b = 0; b < 10; ++b)
      grid_rows.push_back(b), grid_category.push_back(c);
  const Tensor gz = nn::take_rows(tn, grid_rows), gc = nn::from_vector(grid_category, {100}),
               gu         = nn::zeros({100, 2});
  const Tensor grid       = sample(gz, gc, gu);
  const double cat_effect = MaxAbsDiff(
      nn::slice_axis(grid, 0, 10, 100), nn::tile(nn::slice_axis(grid, 0, 0, 10), {9, 1}));
  SaveArrays(
      (root / "category_traversal.npz").string(),
      {{"z", gz}, {"category", gc}, {"continuous", gu}, {"fake", grid}});
  Mosaic(root / "category_traversal.png", grid, 10);
  double cont_effect = 0;
  for (int axis = 0; axis < 2; ++axis) {
    std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
    std::vector<float>        u(55 * 2, 0.f);
    for (int b = 0; b < 5; ++b)
      for (int k = 0; k < 11; ++k)
        rows.push_back(b), u[(b * 11 + k) * 2 + axis] = -1.f + .2f * k;
    const Tensor z = nn::take_rows(tn, rows), c = nn::zeros({55}, nn::DType::Int32),
                 uu     = nn::from_vector(u, {55, 2});
    const Tensor images = sample(z, c, uu);
    for (int b = 0; b < 5; ++b)
      cont_effect = std::max(
          cont_effect,
          MaxAbsDiff(nn::take_rows(images, {b * 11 + 10}), nn::take_rows(images, {b * 11})));
    const auto name = "continuous" + std::to_string(axis);
    SaveArrays(
        (root / (name + "_traversal.npz")).string(),
        {{"z", z}, {"category", c}, {"continuous", uu}, {"fake", images}});
    Mosaic(root / (name + "_traversal.png"), images, 11);
  }
  Require(
      cat_effect > 1e-5 && cont_effect > 1e-5,
      "both generated code paths affect pixels, not semantic certification");
  int  invalid = 0;
  auto bad_c   = grid_category;
  for (int k : {-1, 10}) {
    bad_c[0] = k;
    try {
      sample(gz, nn::from_vector(bad_c, {100}), gu);
    } catch (const std::exception&) {
      ++invalid;
    }
  }
  std::vector<float> bad_u(200, 0.f);
  bad_u[0] = 2;
  try {
    sample(gz, gc, nn::from_vector(bad_u, {100, 2}));
  } catch (const std::exception&) {
    ++invalid;
  }
  Require(invalid == 3, "invalid codes rejected");
  Require(Equal(before, restored_arrays()), "all inference immutable");
  Mosaic(root / "generated.png", nn::slice_axis(repeat, 0, 0, 40), 8);

  const auto best = nn::cast(nn::argmax(output.at("q_probability"), 1), nn::DType::Int64)
                        .to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto truth    = nn::cast(tc.category, nn::DType::Int64).to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  double     accuracy = 0;
  for (int b = 0; b < 200; ++b)
    accuracy += best[b] == truth[b];
  const double mse = nn::mean(
                         nn::square(
                             nn::cast(tc.continuous, nn::DType::Float64) -
                             nn::cast(output.at("q_mean"), nn::DType::Float64)))
                         .item();
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":77469,\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"steps_per_group\":" << steps
       << ",\"optimizer_updates\":" << 3 * steps << ",\"selected_epoch_fixed_final\":" << epochs
       << ",\"generated_category_recognition_accuracy\":" << accuracy / 200
       << ",\"generated_continuous_recognition_mse\":" << mse
       << ",\"category_pixel_max_effect\":" << cat_effect
       << ",\"continuous_pixel_max_effect\":" << cont_effect
       << ",\"single_batch_max_error\":" << parity;
  for (auto key :
       {"discriminator_loss",
        "generator_loss",
        "recognition_loss",
        "categorical_loss",
        "continuous_loss",
        "mi_lower_bound",
        "pixel_mmd"})
    meta << ",\"test_" << key << "\":" << Value(output, key);
  meta << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";
  Require(bool(meta) && bool(history) && bool(batches), "complete artifacts");
  history.close();
  batches.close();
  meta.close();
  std::cout << "fixed final=" << epochs << ", category accuracy=" << accuracy / 200
            << ", continuous MSE=" << mse << ", MI bound=" << Value(output, "mi_lower_bound")
            << "; D then Q then G/restore/imageOnlyQ/codeOnlyG/immutable PASS (training " << seconds
            << " s)\nArtifacts: " << root.string() << "\nAll infogan checks passed.\n";
  std::ifstream input(root / "history.tsv");
  std::string   header;
  std::getline(input, header);
  std::vector<double> axis, dl, gl, rl;
  double              epoch, a, b, r, bound, mmd;
  while (input >> epoch >> a >> b >> r >> bound >> mmd) {
    axis.push_back(epoch);
    dl.push_back(a);
    gl.push_back(b);
    rl.push_back(r);
  }
  const double high = std::max(
      {*std::max_element(dl.begin(), dl.end()),
       *std::max_element(gl.begin(), gl.end()),
       *std::max_element(rl.begin(), rl.end())});
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(0, 1.4 * high)
      .lines(axis, dl, "Validation D", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .points(axis, dl, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4.)
      .lines(axis, gl, "Validation G total", {220, 38, 38}, 2.)
      .points(axis, gl, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4.)
      .lines(axis, rl, "Validation Q recognition", {22, 163, 74}, 2.)
      .points(axis, rl, "", {22, 163, 74}, 4.)
      .x_label("Completed epoch; fixed final3")
      .y_label("Separate minimized objectives")
      .title("Three logged objectives; no checkpoint selection")
      .save_svg("build/infogan_learning.svg");
}
```
