> Both native source and recognition partials enter G

On the unchanged initial minibatch, the program differentiates three fresh forwards with
respect to G alone: source loss, recognition R, and their sum. The component arrays sum
to the total within native Float32 rounding; the total matches the frozen26800 G derivative
values exactly. Both component norms are positive. Q therefore sends a learning signal
through its image input into G, despite having a separate parameter store.
The norm comparison measures the initial signal size only, not quality, improvement,
semantic disentanglement or the eventual relative effect of Adam's normalized updates.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/infogan_g_partials.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/infogan/initial_g_partials.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  std::vector<double>      norms;
  std::vector<std::string> names{"source_generator_loss", "recognition_loss", "generator_loss"};
  for (const auto& name : names) {
    double squared = 0;
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key.rfind(name + "/", 0) == 0)
        squared += n::sum(n::square(n::cast(value, n::DType::Float64))).item();
    norms.push_back(std::sqrt(squared));
  }
  std::print(
      "| initial G partial | L2 norm |\n|---|---:|\n| source |{:.12f}|\n| recognition |{:.12f}|\n| "
      "total |{:.12f}|\n",
      norms[0],
      norms[1],
      norms[2]);
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points({0}, {norms[0]}, "G source partial", {37, 99, 235}, 6.)
      .points({1}, {norms[1]}, "G recognition partial", {22, 163, 74}, 6.)
      .x_limits(-.4, 1.4)
      .y_limits(0, 1.6 * std::max(norms[0], norms[1]))
      .x_label("0 source;1 recognition; initial32-row batch")
      .y_label("L2 norm over all26800 G derivatives")
      .title("Two distinct objectives send gradients into G")
      .save_svg("build/infogan_g_partials.svg");
}
