> Change one continuous code while holding everything else fixed

Each row fixes one of five noise vectors, category 0 and the other continuous coordinate 0.
Eleven columns sweep the selected coordinate from-1 to 1. The source computes those levels
as Float32(-1+.2*k), preserving its rounding. Across both55-image traversals, endpoint
changes reach .0916647315 in a pixel. This proves that a continuous input path matters;
it does not show rotation, thickness, independence of semantic factors or generalization
outside the training support. The source rejects codes outside[-1,1].

