> A negative empirical variational score leaves true information unknown

The expected information objective uses H(prior)+E log Q(code|G(noise,code)). Its variational
form is explained in [InfoGAN section 5](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03657). This program
estimates the expectation with generated rows; it does not compute the true posterior or
true mutual information. A finite-batch score has sampling error and is not a certified
bound for this particular sample. Here it remains negative through validation and on test.
Its negative value alone cannot establish positive true information. Actual information
and semantic interpretation remain unverified; code dependence is checked separately.
The zero line is a reference, not a fitted threshold or checkpoint-selection rule.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/infogan_bound.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream in("build/infogan/history.tsv");
  std::string   header;
  std::getline(in, header);
  std::vector<double> x, y;
  double              epoch, d, g, r, bound, mmd;
  while (in >> epoch >> d >> g >> r >> bound >> mmd) {
    x.push_back(epoch);
    y.push_back(bound);
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(x, y, "Empirical validation score", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4.)
      .lines({1, 3}, {0, 0}, "", {100, 116, 139}, 1.)
      .y_limits(-1.2, .3)
      .x_label("Completed epoch; no selection")
      .y_label("Fixed prior entropy minus recognition R")
      .title("A negative variational score is not negative mutual information")
      .save_svg("build/infogan_bound.svg");
}
