> Code recovery, pixel dependence and image quality are different questions

On200 generated test samples, Q recovers the supplied prior category with accuracy .115,
compared with .1 expected for uniform random guesses. This is a small descriptive result,
without an uncertainty estimate or claim of improvement. It is not MNIST digit recognition.
Q's continuous means give per-coordinate MSE .2307212418466 against the supplied codes.
A fixed zero prediction gives the finite-prior reference computed below; its population
reference under uniform[-1,1] is1/3. Neither quantity measures realistic digits.

The same block also computes a deliberately constant image reference from fitting pixels
only. Its coarse MMD is much lower than G's, despite having zero diversity. This diagnostic
blind spot is why the actual generated galleries, code traversals and recognition metrics
stay separate. No baseline, MMD or test statistic chooses the fitted checkpoint.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/infogan_mse.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a, prior;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/infogan/outputs.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/infogan/test_prior.npz"))
    prior.emplace(k, v);
  auto target            = n::cast(prior.at("continuous"), n::DType::Float64),
       mean              = n::cast(a.at("q_mean"), n::DType::Float64);
  const double predicted = n::mean(n::square(target - mean)).item(),
               zero      = n::mean(n::square(target)).item();
  const auto best =
      n::cast(n::argmax(a.at("q_probability"), 1), n::DType::Int64).to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto truth   = prior.at("category").to_vector<std::int32_t>();
  double     correct = 0;
  for (std::size_t row = 0; row < best.size(); ++row)
    correct += best[row] == truth[row];
  const double accuracy = correct / double(best.size()),
               chance   = 1. / double(a.at("q_probability").size(1));
  std::print(
      "| code diagnostic | value |\n|---|---:|\n| generated-category accuracy |{:.3f}|\n| uniform "
      "guessing expectation |{:.3f}|\n| Q continuous coordinate MSE |{:.14f}|\n| fixed zero "
      "continuous "
      "MSE |{:.14f}|\n",
      accuracy,
      chance,
      predicted,
      zero);
  auto pools =
      n::models::LoadSaliency(std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency");
  auto constant = n::tile(n::mean(pools[0].images.reshape({1000, 784}), {0}, true), {200, 1});
  const double baseline =
      n::models::ImqMmd(
          n::models::GanCoarsePixels(pools[2].images), n::models::GanCoarsePixels(constant))
          .value.item();
  std::print(
      "| image diagnostic | coarse MMD² |\n|---|---:|\n| G fixed samples |{:.12f}|\n| repeated "
      "fitting mean |{:.12f}|\n",
      a.at("pixel_mmd").item(),
      baseline);
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points({0, 1}, {predicted, zero}, "", {37, 99, 235}, 6.)
      .x_limits(-.4, 1.4)
      .y_limits(0, 1.4 * std::max(predicted, zero))
      .x_label("0 image-only Q;1 fixed zero mean")
      .y_label("MSE per continuous coordinate")
      .title("Continuous-code recovery against a fixed zero prediction")
      .save_svg("build/infogan_mse.svg");
}
