> Verification and remaining limits

The native-delegated unchanged original and this complete report each preserve all eleven
original archives/684712 values in dtype, shape and value bytes, both TSV files, all four
source PNGs and every non-timing JSON value. Duration is remeasured. All14 checkpoint
tensors restore exactly; image-only Q equals the full-forward Q fields, standalone
code/noise-only G equals its full-forward output, and single/batch maximum error is0.
All traversal, generation and recognition calls leave every G/D/Q weight unchanged.

The independent NumPy oracle imports no datamunge and performs no fitting. It checks
516984 forward/control values, all 77469 initial parameter derivatives,39 scalar finite
differences,30800 exact prior/noise values and every one of the3000 fitting-row visits.
The report additionally archives80400 native G component derivatives; an independent
matrix-calculus check selects source and recognition terms through their independent
D/Q Jacobians, and checks all three G banks. The26800 total G derivatives also match the
frozen initial derivative archive exactly. The program separately verifies native Q-partial
independence from the D write and selected-store ownership of the first three phases.

Native, Python and R checks cover exact prior words and forced rejection, default parameter
census, separate image-only Q, owned records, malformed inputs, strides and applicable
continuous first/higher paths. Component coverage does not complete independent Python/R
full experiment loops. This is one fixed short run, without a seed sweep, paper-scale image
benchmark, uncertainty interval, proof of convergence or demonstrated semantic factors.

Reference: [Chen, Duan, Houthooft, Schulman, Sutskever and Abbeel (2016), InfoGAN:
Interpretable Representation Learning by Information Maximizing Generative Adversarial Nets](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03657).
The exact dense widths, separate unit-variance Q, explicit RNG protocol, schedule and
artifacts follow the repository teaching source. Canonical native tensor maps, stable source
loss, categorical CE, explicit generated priors and recognition objectives provide the API.
